:"4ef47a70be37fc44d2bf10a373274be2150b652c","position":"1788987420416566001-8804e247-af35-4485-ab0b-533e452fb356"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"11f9fa7da1fdfd00185ec1ea9ebb944f6faa8a5cca9e2bb0c35f5ea932960569","event_uuid":"6776b1c0-252d-40dd-ab50-0595984dab10","position":{"commit_sha":"e993fb5eac94aeb1e4f59c40dfe72b9e98e66b97","position":"1788988371330288001-6776b1c0-252d-40dd-ab50-0595984dab10"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"77be954e5b6f03cdd7f5fcea1c28a220eab1d29ff1de1f07f3230c9c2a6e7f29","event_uuid":"e22c48e0-3ef7-4f9e-b012-69b6d74289d3","position":{"commit_sha":"8274240583eda3e408c5ebfd91332704827f1c70","position":"1788989188115891001-e22c48e0-3ef7-4f9e-b012-69b6d74289d3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Interim RCA/update: live host checks found review-bot webhook 401s from Gerrit container IP 172.21.0.4 after the token rotation, while SSM, compose .env, running review-bot env, and rebar.git refs/meta/config:webhooks.config now all hash to the same token (03a77b8c96ff...). Gerrit was restarted at 2026-09-09T12:50:31Z; review-bot at 12:20:18Z. Working hypothesis: the stale-secret interval was a Gerrit/webhooks reload gap during rotation; the class fix is to make inbound webhook auth rejects observable instead of allowing /review/health to stay green. RED evidence: new tests failed because /health lacked webhook_auth_rejections and observability.sh published no reviewbot_webhook_auth_rejections metric. GREEN targeted evidence so far: review-bot app/script/alarm tests pass (159 passed targeted).","timestamp":1788958890460864001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA confirmation update: fresh smoke at 2026-09-09T13:07:50Z (admin comment on scratch change 2909) produced Gerrit webhooks plugin error 'Exceeded max retries(3). Reason: {\"status\":\"unauthorized\"}' and review-bot 401 from Gerrit container IP 172.21.0.4. Token hashes match across SSM, compose .env, review-bot GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN, and refs/meta/config, which falsifies 'current stored token mismatch'. Source check of the Gerrit 3.14 webhooks plugin shows RemoteConfig reads url/event/timeouts/ssl only, and the event processor sends built-in X-Origin-Url; it does not read our configured header = X-Rebar-Token. Confirmed root cause: previous header-token hardening relied on a plugin feature that is absent/ignored, so after the URL token was removed Gerrit could never authenticate webhooks. Fix in progress: accept Gerrit's private compose-network webhook path by built-in X-Origin-Url/no public X-Forwarded-For, keep public /review/* token auth, expose rejection counter in /health + CloudWatch alarm, and update ADR/runbook/webhooks template. Full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2 is running now.","timestamp":1788965499984812001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA + fix pushed: live webhook 401s were not a stale-token mismatch after normalization; SSM, review-bot env, and refs/meta/config token hashes matched. A fresh smoke comment still produced webhooks-plugin 401s. Root cause: the deployed Gerrit 3.14 webhooks plugin ignores arbitrary 'header = X-Rebar-Token' config, so Gerrit never sent the token the hardened receiver required. RED coverage added: review-bot health exposes webhook auth rejections while liveness stays 200, Gerrit's internal X-Origin-Url path is accepted without unsupported header, public spoof via X-Forwarded-For is rejected, and observability publishes per-interval rejection deltas. Fix b52c9d440b27d pushed as Gerrit change 2928. Validation: targeted 179 passed; full 'make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2' passed with GIT_CONFIG_* unset.","timestamp":1788971744275176001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Update: remediation for Gerrit change 2928 has been amended and pushed as PS3 after a full local `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` pass with GIT_CONFIG_* unset. PS3 tightens the internal Gerrit webhook path so tokenless acceptance requires the canonical Gerrit origin, no public forwarding headers, and the TCP peer resolving to the configured internal Gerrit service; it also fixes the auth-rejection metric reset behavior and updates the ADR/runbook/docs drift. Awaiting Gerrit LLM-Review and Verified votes before deploy/close.","timestamp":1788983119079444001}],"created_at":1788913944867484001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f4a2f81e-f8f0-43e7-ae69-31233beed4f3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8ea3-3750-6772-4ac6"},{"link_uuid":"88f4a40c-2c7d-411d-bd36-70bcdc868a88","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d24d-b178-f39e-4771"},{"link_uuid":"a2be202e-12ae-486f-8263-80966660e739","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4667-690a-ead3-445e"},{"link_uuid":"7b0ef17b-5b66-40ab-b45e-300bd1239ce7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"75b7-06ec-7d99-4994"}],"description":"## Context\nAfter the review-bot token rotation, Gerrit-originated webhooks were still rejected with `review-bot webhook: rejected (missing/invalid token)` even though `/review/health` was 200 and manual authenticated `/review/rerun` calls with the SSM token could vote.\n\n## RCA plan and findings\n1. Compare the public-token path only: hash (never print) SSM `GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN`/`WEBHOOK_TOKEN` inputs against the review-bot container environment to rule out stale public-caller credentials.\n2. Ground the Gerrit delivery path in the deployed artifact before relying on it: inspect the exact Gerrit 3.14 webhooks plugin source/JAR class used on the host for request headers, then trigger a live scratch delivery and capture only redacted receiver/log evidence that the concrete header name/value class is present. The observed plugin header is Gerrit's built-in `X-Origin-Url`; if that header is absent or renamed, do not ship the tokenless path--instead keep Gerrit deliveries rejected and open a follow-up to add a supported authenticated producer/proxy header mechanism.\n3. Verify the remaining internal-origin auth inputs: configured canonical web URL, internal Gerrit base URL, absence of public forwarding headers, and compose-network peer resolution used by the receiver.\n4. Trigger live scratch `patchset-created` and `comment-added` deliveries and prove the observable outcome without leaking secrets: Gerrit deliveries are accepted/queued by `/webhook` (HTTP 202/no new 401) through the verified internal-origin path, not by proving an `X-Rebar-Token` header that the deployed plugin cannot send.\n5. Fix the confirmed class: keep token auth for public receiver callers; accept tokenless Gerrit-originated webhooks only when the verified `X-Origin-Url` matches configured Gerrit URLs, no public `X-Forwarded-For` is present, and the TCP peer resolves to the configured internal Gerrit service host; expose auth rejections via health + CloudWatch so a future auth break pages instead of leaving liveness green.\n6. Keep all `/review/health` consumers in sync: `src/rebar/review_bot/app.py`, `infra/scripts/observability.sh`, `infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf`, `tests/unit/test_review_bot*.py`, and `tests/scripts/test_observability_reviewbot_webhook_auth.py`.\n7. Update the rotation/runbook and Gerrit config docs to state that `infra/gerrit/webhooks.config` carries no secret/header, the Gerrit plugin does not support arbitrary `header =` auth, and the rotation smoke must verify a live accepted Gerrit delivery plus public-token `/review/rerun` behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Public-token inputs are compared by redacted hashes, and stale public caller credentials are either fixed or ruled out.\n- [ ] The deployed Gerrit webhooks plugin source/JAR inspection identifies the concrete built-in origin header it emits, or records that none exists and blocks the tokenless-path fix.\n- [ ] A live scratch delivery confirms the concrete origin header is present using redacted evidence only.\n- [ ] The deployed Gerrit webhooks plugin capability is documented: it does not emit `X-Rebar-Token`; it emits the verified built-in origin header.\n- [ ] A live scratch `patchset-created` delivery is accepted by `/webhook` via the internal-origin path, with evidence recorded as status/metric/log lines that do not print secrets.\n- [ ] A live scratch `comment-added` delivery is accepted by `/webhook` via the internal-origin path, with evidence recorded as status/metric/log lines that do not print secrets.\n- [ ] Public `/review/*` callers still require `X-Rebar-Token` or the legacy redacted token parameter.\n- [ ] Public spoof attempts with origin headers are rejected when they carry a forwarded-client marker or do not come from the configured Gerrit service peer.\n- [ ] `/health` exposes webhook auth rejection count and age while ordinary liveness remains 200.\n- [ ] `observability.sh` publishes a per-interval `reviewbot_webhook_auth_rejections` metric without losing increments across review-bot restarts or failed CloudWatch publishes.\n- [ ] Terraform declares an alarm for nonzero webhook auth rejections.\n- [ ] Review-bot ops, token-rotation, Gerrit setup, and ADR docs describe the current internal-origin/public-token split.\n- [ ] Regression tests fail before the fix and pass after it, including internal-origin acceptance, public spoof rejection, health payload, observability delta, and restart/reset behavior.\n- [ ] Full `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` passes with the documented `GIT_CONFIG_*` variables unset before Gerrit review.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/app.py","reason":"Expose recent webhook auth rejection state in health payload for observability."},{"path":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","reason":"Publish operator-visible webhook auth failure metric/alarm input."},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"Document token rotation reload and webhook smoke-test procedure."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot.py","reason":"Pin health payload/rejection counter behavior."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_observability_timeout_9313.py","reason":"Pin observability publication for webhook auth failure if needed."},{"path":"infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf","reason":"Declare CloudWatch alarm if the new metric is alarmed in Terraform."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4667-690a-ead3-445e"],["relates_to","75b7-06ec-7d99-4994"],["relates_to","d24d-b178-f39e-4771"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c557468d-6d50-4b99-a851-391d9cf94f70","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ops","review-bot"],"ticket_id":"073f-b86f-42c6-456f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gerrit webhooks still emit missing-or-invalid token rejects after rotation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cd313aba-6c27-4959-b091-9630da6a09d5","a5215797-251d-4482-9864-3e9db8475140","c557468d-6d50-4b99-a851-391d9cf94f70","4db4ddb9-fd6a-4566-8ec9-7ef7fbb0afe9","12e20133-f7ce-44d4-bdfa-26aa9a26647f","c2d5662e-cb77-419c-a300-c6f5e5e7ee81","4e087b17-4d19-4160-9fdd-6a40de039f6e","88f4a40c-2c7d-411d-bd36-70bcdc868a88","a2be202e-12ae-486f-8263-80966660e739","b120c043-9966-422c-af33-10d900e91987","7b0ef17b-5b66-40ab-b45e-300bd1239ce7","d2f5690b-550e-4a5f-af55-6e7e6ff0832c","8804e247-af35-4485-ab0b-533e452fb356","6776b1c0-252d-40dd-ab50-0595984dab10","e22c48e0-3ef7-4f9e-b012-69b6d74289d3"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788994496445775001,"uuid":"7a19a038-7701-4b76-83e6-c183e63206cd"}